        ("Soft Skills", "In critical thinking, which logical fallacy involves attacking the character or motive of the opponent rather than addressing the substance of their argument?", "Straw Man", "Ad Hominem", "Post Hoc Ergo Propter Hoc", "False Dilemma", "Ad Hominem"),
        ("Soft Skills", "According to the revised Bloom's Taxonomy (Anderson & Krathwohl, 2001), which cognitive process represents the highest order of thinking?", "Evaluate", "Analyze", "Create", "Apply", "Create"),
        ("Soft Skills", "Malcolm Knowles' theory of 'Andragogy' relies on several core assumptions about adult learners. Which of the following is a primary assumption?", "Adults are primarily motivated by external pressures and grades.", "Adults enter the educational process with a subject-centered orientation.", "The adult's self-concept moves from dependency toward self-direction.", "Adults have less experiential foundation than younger learners.", "The adult's self-concept moves from dependency toward self-direction."),
        ("Soft Skills", "Daniel Goleman's framework for Emotional Intelligence (EQ) comprises five key components. Which of the following is NOT one of them?", "Self-Awareness", "Cognitive Fluidity", "Empathy", "Social Skills", "Cognitive Fluidity"),
        ("Soft Skills", "The phenomenon of 'Groupthink', coined by Irving Janis, is most likely to occur under which conditions?", "High group cohesiveness, isolation from outside influences, and directive leadership.", "Low group cohesiveness and high task ambiguity.", "Diverse group membership and democratic leadership.", "Virtual teams communicating strictly asynchronously.", "High group cohesiveness, isolation from outside influences, and directive leadership."),
        ("Soft Skills", "In Herzberg's Two-Factor Theory of motivation, which of the following is considered a 'Hygiene Factor' rather than a 'Motivator'?", "Recognition for achievement", "The work itself", "Career advancement opportunities", "Salary and working conditions", "Salary and working conditions"),
        ("Soft Skills", "Victor Vroom's Expectancy Theory posits that motivation is a product of three variables: Expectancy, Instrumentality, and what?", "Valence", "Equity", "Achievement", "Affiliation", "Valence"),
        ("Soft Skills", "The 'Fundamental Attribution Error' describes the cognitive tendency to:", "Overemphasize situational factors when explaining someone else's behavior.", "Overemphasize dispositional (internal) traits when explaining someone else's behavior.", "Attribute one's own success to internal factors and failure to external factors.", "Assume others share the same beliefs and values as oneself.", "Overemphasize dispositional (internal) traits when explaining someone else's behavior."),
        ("Soft Skills", "Leon Festinger's theory of Cognitive Dissonance primarily deals with the psychological discomfort that arises when:", "An individual is faced with an unsolvable logical paradox.", "An individual holds two or more contradictory beliefs, ideas, or values.", "A subordinate disagrees with a superior but cannot speak up.", "A group cannot reach a consensus.", "An individual holds two or more contradictory beliefs, ideas, or values."),
        ("Soft Skills", "According to the Hersey-Blanchard Situational Leadership model, the most effective leadership style depends primarily on:", "The complexity of the task at hand.", "The leader's innate personality traits.", "The maturity or readiness level of the followers.", "The organizational culture and hierarchical structure.", "The maturity or readiness level of the followers."),
        ("Soft Skills", "In Kantian ethics (Deontology), the 'Categorical Imperative' dictates that one should:", "Always act to maximize the greatest good for the greatest number.", "Act only according to that maxim whereby you can, at the same time, will that it should become a universal law.", "Always act in accordance with the laws of the local jurisdiction.", "Judge the morality of an action solely by its consequences.", "Act only according to that maxim whereby you can, at the same time, will that it should become a universal law."),
        ("Soft Skills", "Anthropologist Edward T. Hall distinguished between 'High-Context' and 'Low-Context' cultures. A 'High-Context' culture relies heavily on:", "Explicit verbal communication and written contracts.", "Direct, assertive negotiation tactics.", "Implicit communication, nonverbal cues, and established relationships.", "Strict adherence to agenda and schedules.", "Implicit communication, nonverbal cues, and established relationships."),
        ("Soft Skills", "The study of 'Kinesics' in nonverbal communication involves the interpretation of:", "Voice quality and tone.", "Body motion, posture, and facial expressions.", "The use of time in communication.", "Touch and tactile interactions.", "Body motion, posture, and facial expressions."),
        ("Soft Skills", "In the context of vocal communication, 'Paralanguage' includes all of the following EXCEPT:", "Pitch and intonation", "Speaking speed", "The literal denotative meaning of the words", "Volume and hesitation noises", "The literal denotative meaning of the words"),
        ("Soft Skills", "The 'Halo Effect' is a cognitive bias where:", "An observer's overall impression of a person influences their feelings about that person's specific traits.", "People tend to remember the first piece of information they hear.", "Individuals believe they are less biased than their peers.", "People overestimate the degree to which others agree with them.", "An observer's overall impression of a person influences their feelings about that person's specific traits."),
        ("Soft Skills", "According to Julian Rotter's psychological concept, an individual with a strong 'Internal Locus of Control' believes that:", "Their life outcomes are determined primarily by fate or luck.", "Their life outcomes are determined primarily by their own actions and decisions.", "Institutional structures dictate their success.", "They are controlled by subconscious desires.", "Their life outcomes are determined primarily by their own actions and decisions."),
        ("Soft Skills", "David McClelland's Theory of Needs identifies three primary motivational drivers. Which of the following is NOT one of them?", "Need for Achievement (nAch)", "Need for Affiliation (nAff)", "Need for Power (nPow)", "Need for Security (nSec)", "Need for Security (nSec)"),
        ("Soft Skills", "The Ishikawa diagram, commonly used in quality management and team problem-solving, is also known as the:", "Pareto Chart", "Gantt Chart", "Fishbone Diagram", "Scatter Plot", "Fishbone Diagram"),
        ("Soft Skills", "In Edward de Bono's 'Six Thinking Hats' methodology for parallel thinking, what does the 'Black Hat' represent?", "Emotional, intuitive responses", "Creative, out-of-the-box ideas", "Cautious, critical judgment and risk assessment", "Process control and organization", "Cautious, critical judgment and risk assessment"),
        ("Soft Skills", "When conducting a SWOT analysis for strategic planning, 'Opportunities' and 'Threats' represent:", "Internal factors inherent to the organization.", "External factors in the environment over which the organization has no direct control.", "Financial metrics.", "Past performance indicators.", "External factors in the environment over which the organization has no direct control."),
        ("Soft Skills", "Parkinson's Law states that:", "80 percent of consequences come from 20 percent of the causes.", "Work expands so as to fill the time available for its completion.", "In a hierarchy, every employee tends to rise to their level of incompetence.", "If anything can go wrong, it will.", "Work expands so as to fill the time available for its completion."),
        ("Soft Skills", "The 'Peter Principle' is an organizational management concept suggesting that:", "Employees are motivated primarily by autonomy, mastery, and purpose.", "Managers tend to promote individuals who share their exact management style.", "In a hierarchy, every employee tends to rise to their level of incompetence.", "Small incremental changes lead to massive long-term results.", "In a hierarchy, every employee tends to rise to their level of incompetence."),
        ("Soft Skills", "In the Johari Window, the 'Blind Area' represents information that is:", "Known to self but unknown to others.", "Known to others but unknown to self.", "Unknown to both self and others.", "Known to both self and others.", "Known to others but unknown to self."),
        ("Soft Skills", "The Delphi Technique is a structured communication method primarily used for:", "Resolving interpersonal conflicts in real-time.", "Brainstorming creative marketing ideas.", "Forecasting and building consensus among a panel of experts through anonymous questionnaires.", "Conducting performance appraisals.", "Forecasting and building consensus among a panel of experts through anonymous questionnaires."),
        ("Soft Skills", "Geert Hofstede's Cultural Dimensions theory includes the 'Power Distance Index' (PDI). A high PDI indicates that:", "The society values extreme egalitarianism.", "The society accepts and expects that power is distributed unequally.", "The society prioritizes individualism over collectivism.", "The society has a low tolerance for uncertainty and ambiguity.", "The society accepts and expects that power is distributed unequally."),
        ("Soft Skills", "In the psychological phenomenon known as the 'Pygmalion Effect', what happens?", "Higher expectations placed upon an individual lead to an increase in their performance.", "Individuals perform worse when they feel they are being heavily scrutinized.", "People tend to conform to the incorrect opinions of the majority.", "Rewards actively decrease intrinsic motivation.", "Higher expectations placed upon an individual lead to an increase in their performance."),
        ("Soft Skills", "The 'Straw Man Fallacy' in argumentation occurs when a speaker:", "Attacks the opponent's personal character.", "Assumes that because two things occurred together, one caused the other.", "Intentionally misrepresents or exaggerates an opponent's position to make it easier to defeat.", "Presents only two completely opposing options when more exist.", "Intentionally misrepresents or exaggerates an opponent's position to make it easier to defeat."),
